{{!-- "Browse by tag" — the pill strip the design draws on both homepage layouts.

	{{> "tag-strip"}}                    A1's: tucked to the right of the section heading, no counts
	{{> "tag-strip" wide=true}}          A2's: a full-width row, each pill carrying its post count

	wide    the A2 sizing and layout

This partial is the homepage's QUERY; the drawing is in tag-pills.hbs, which the tag archive's
"Other tags" strip shares over a query of its own.

The strip wraps; it does not scroll. That is the `strip` utility's whole job, and the reasoning
— a hidden scrollbar reads as absent content, and an overflow container crops the focus ring on
the pill inside it — is in src/styles/main.css beside the utility.

WHICH TAGS. The design source hardcodes eight, ordered by post count. Here the order and the
membership are the publication's own: the eight tags with the most posts, which is the only
"top tags" a theme can mean. A publication with fewer than eight renders fewer; the pills wrap
rather than scroll, so no count breaks the row.

`limit="8"` rather than `"all"` is deliberate — Ghost 6 caps every {{#get}} at 100 silently
(core/shared/max-limit-cap.js) and this strip is a taste of the filing system, not the Tags
Directory, which is the Surface that lists all of them.

Two things about the reads below, both of which cost a capture run to learn:

- `../wide`, not `wide`. {{#get}} renders its block with the query's response as the context, so
  a partial argument passed to THIS partial is one frame up from inside the block. Read as `wide`
  it is undefined, and the A2 homepage silently renders A1's right-tucked strip. (`{{#if}}` does
  not add a frame of its own — Handlebars only pushes one when the context object changes — so
  one `../` is right even nested inside the guard below.)
- `{{#if tags}}` and not the get's `{{else}}`. get calls `options.inverse` only for an invalid
  resource or an API error (core/frontend/helpers/get.js), never for an empty result, so a
  publication with no public tags would otherwise render the label and a rule with nothing after
  them. Same shape as post/related.hbs. --}}
{{#get "tags" include="count.posts" order="count.posts desc" limit="8" as |tags|}}
	{{#if tags}}
		{{> "tag-pills" tags=tags label=(t "Browse by tag") wide=../wide}}
	{{/if}}
{{/get}}
